<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. Pursuant to the CIRP under the IBC, 2016 initiated by the NCLT on 24 July 2018  approved the Plan submitted by the consortium of JSW Steel Limited &amp; AION Investments Private II Limited, which, resulted in the following:  n(a)Extinguishment of 5,07,32,841 equity shares of Rs. 10 each and 1,75,00,000 preference shares of Rs. 100 each held by the erstwhile promoters.  n(b)Reduction in the face value of the balance 36,52,33,620 equity shares (including the equity shares issued under (c) and (d) below) held by the non- promoter equity shareholders to Rs. 3.30 per share and their consolidation into 12,05,27,534 equity shares of Rs. 10 each.   n(c)Settlement of debts of financial creditors amounting to Rs. 10,247.86 crores, partly by issue of 20,00,56,892 equity shares of Rs. 10 each, partly by cash payment of Rs. 2,457.00 crores, and partly by the effective purchase of the remaining debt, (on deemed conversion into Optionally Convertible Preference shares), for a sum of Rs. 199.85 crores by a company of the consortium, Milloret Steel Limited (MSL).  n(d)Settlement of corporate guarantees issued to financial creditors amounting to Rs 767.05 crores, partly by issue of 1,51,41,327 equity shares of Rs. 10 each and cash payment of Rs. 20.07 crores.  n(e)Settlement of operational creditors, (other than employees and workmen) for a sum of Rs. 25 crores payable by the Company within one year from the Order date and extinguishment of other current and non-current liabilities standing as on the commencement of Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process.  n(f)Extinguishment of all contingent liabilities, commitments and other claims and obligations including all taxes and other government dues standing as on the effective date (i.e. 31 August 2018).  n(g)Merger of MSL into the Company, resulting in the extinguishment of the deemed Optionally Convertible Preference shares, contemporaneously with (c) above. The shareholders of MSL were issued 34,90,20,000 equity shares of Rs 10 each and 52,59,80,000 Compulsorily Convertible preference shares of Rs 10 each.  n  n2. Exceptional items for the year ended 31 March 2019 comprise of:  n  n(a)Impairment of property plant and equipment amounting to Rs.2,429.75 crores in standalone &amp; Rs.2601.81 crores in consolidated results, which has been recognized based on the recoverable value of these assets.   n(b)Impairment of investments, inventories, receivables, current and non-current assets aggregating to Rs. 1,484.95 crores in standalone &amp; Rs.1418.76 crores in consolidated results, considered not realizable.  n(c)Write back of current and non-current liabilities, including those described in Note 1 above, aggregating to Rs. 1,173.78 crores in standalone &amp; Rs.1191.90 crores in consolidated results.  n(d)Plant Startup Expenses of Rs 27.00 crores incurred in the current quarter which comprise of various one-time revenue expenses incurred for startup of manufacturing facilities at Raigarh plant of the Company which were non-operational for a long period of time.  ntt  nt  nRefer PDF for more details on notes.  n </in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
